1309
01:40:57,262 --> 01:41:01,220
Okay, so let's zoom out for a second. Where has Gemini been heading lately?

1310
01:41:01,486 --> 01:41:04,400
For a while now, Google's been pushing Gemini everywhere.

1311
01:41:04,560 --> 01:41:07,120
Your phone, search, Google Docs, Gmail.

1312
01:41:07,280 --> 01:41:13,440
It slowly stopped being just a chatbot and started being this helper that lives inside the tools you already use every day.

1313
01:41:13,806 --> 01:41:15,520
But voice was always the weak spot.

1314
01:41:15,694 --> 01:41:17,120
Talking to it felt clunky.

1315
01:41:17,280 --> 01:41:19,972
You'd ask a question and it would freeze up while it worked.

1316
01:41:20,160 --> 01:41:22,640
These two new models are Google's answer to that.

1317
01:41:22,926 --> 01:41:28,640
They're built on Gemini 3 Pro, so they're smart, but now they can actually hold a real conversation with you.

1318
01:41:28,942 --> 01:41:30,240
So what can they actually do?

1319
01:41:30,542 --> 01:41:31,332
Here's the big one.

1320
01:41:31,520 --> 01:41:33,680
They can do a task while they're still talking to you.

1321
01:41:34,094 --> 01:41:35,840
Old voice AI work like this.

1322
01:41:36,078 --> 01:41:38,400
You ask, it stops, it goes silent.

1323
01:41:38,574 --> 01:41:41,028
It does the thing behind the scenes, then it comes back.

1324
01:41:41,262 --> 01:41:43,760
That silent gap is the dead air I mentioned at the start.

1325
01:41:44,110 --> 01:41:46,240
Gemini 3.8 Live doesn't do that.

1326
01:41:46,478 --> 01:41:51,440
It can say, let me check that for you, and then actually check in the background while it keeps chatting with you.

1327
01:41:51,662 --> 01:41:53,920
No dead air, no wondering if it hung up.

1328
01:41:54,080 --> 01:41:56,080
Extended thinking takes it even further.

1329
01:41:56,334 --> 01:42:00,160
For a harder task, it thinks through the steps and talks you through them as it goes.

1330
01:42:00,462 --> 01:42:02,240
Like a real person working out loud.

1331
01:42:02,446 --> 01:42:04,388
Let me give you the features that stood out to me.

1332
01:42:04,560 --> 01:42:06,080
First, background tasks.

1333
01:42:06,318 --> 01:42:09,520
It can run tools and look things up while the conversation keeps flowing.

1334
01:42:09,742 --> 01:42:12,480
That's the main trick, and it's the one that changes everything.

1335
01:42:12,720 --> 01:42:14,000
Second, it can see.

1336
01:42:14,190 --> 01:42:18,400
You can show it something live, through a camera, and it uses what it sees to answer you.

1337
01:42:18,510 --> 01:42:21,828
So it understands what you say and what you're looking at at the same time.

1338
01:42:23,470 --> 01:42:25,840
Third, it's sharp with codes and numbers.

1339
01:42:26,030 --> 01:42:28,640
Confirmation codes, claim numbers, that kind of thing.

1340
01:42:28,910 --> 01:42:31,200
The stuff old voice AI always got wrong.

1341
01:42:31,440 --> 01:42:32,720
Fourth, languages.

1342
01:42:32,880 --> 01:42:38,240
It handles over 97 of them, and it can switch mid-conversation without you flipping a single setting.

1343
01:42:38,446 --> 01:42:39,440
It just follows along.

1344
01:42:39,630 --> 01:42:43,040
Fifth, on extended thinking, you can control how hard it thinks.

1345
01:42:43,278 --> 01:42:44,560
Light thinking for quick stuff.

1346
01:42:44,782 --> 01:42:46,320
Deeper thinking for the tricky stuff.

1347
01:42:46,606 --> 01:42:47,200
Your call.

1348
01:42:47,374 --> 01:42:49,360
Now here's the part I found really clever.

1349
01:42:49,520 --> 01:42:51,360
How does this actually work under the hood?

1350
01:42:51,566 --> 01:42:53,680
Old voice setups were like a relay race.

1351
01:42:53,902 --> 01:42:57,280
One model turned your speech into text, another model did the thinking.

1352
01:42:57,518 --> 01:42:59,520
A third turned the answer back into speech.

1353
01:42:59,694 --> 01:43:00,640
Three handoffs.

1354
01:43:00,846 --> 01:43:04,000
And every handoff added delay and made things more likely to break.

1355
01:43:04,270 --> 01:43:07,360
Gemini 3.8 Live throws that whole relay out.

1356
01:43:07,598 --> 01:43:10,560
It's one model that hears audio and speaks audio directly.

1357
01:43:10,734 --> 01:43:12,080
One step instead of three.

1358
01:43:12,302 --> 01:43:14,240
That's why it feels faster and more natural.

1359
01:43:14,414 --> 01:43:16,560
Fewer moving parts, less to go wrong.

1360
01:43:16,720 --> 01:43:22,212
And one more thing worth knowing, every bit of audio it makes is watermarked with something called synth ID.

1361
01:43:22,400 --> 01:43:28,420
You can't hear it, but it marks the audio as AI made. That's Google being upfront about what's real and what isn't.

1362
01:43:28,800 --> 01:43:30,400
So who is this actually for?

1363
01:43:30,640 --> 01:43:34,640
