1370
01:44:04,000 --> 01:44:05,280
Why does this matter though?

1371
01:44:05,440 --> 01:44:06,916
Why should you actually care?

1372
01:44:07,120 --> 01:44:12,708
Because voice is finally becoming a real way to work, not a gimmick you try once and drop.

1373
01:44:13,824 --> 01:44:19,492
For years, talking to AI meant repeating yourself, waiting through pauses, and giving up halfway.

1374
01:44:19,744 --> 01:44:21,540
It was faster to just type.

1375
01:44:21,744 --> 01:44:22,944
That flips now.

1376
01:44:23,104 --> 01:44:30,660
When the AI can talk and work at the same time, it stops feeling like a machine and starts feeling like a helper sitting right next to you.

1377
01:44:30,944 --> 01:44:34,692
And once you feel that, going back to typing everything out feels slow.

1378
01:44:35,104 --> 01:44:36,624
Now let me save you some pain.

1379
01:44:36,864 --> 01:44:39,620
Here are the mistakes people are already making with this.

1380
01:44:39,984 --> 01:44:43,104
Mistake one, treating it like old voice typing.

1381
01:44:43,264 --> 01:44:47,664
It's not. It's a full conversation partner that can actually go and do things.

1382
01:44:47,904 --> 01:44:55,716
If you use it like a dictation tool, you're wasting most of what it can do. Mistake two, reaching for the heavy model every single time.

1383
01:44:56,064 --> 01:45:00,544
Extended thinking is powerful, but it's built for hard, multi-step jobs.

1384
01:45:00,846 --> 01:45:06,468
For quick, everyday chats, the regular 3.8 live is faster and made for exactly that.

1385
01:45:06,830 --> 01:45:08,356
Match the model to the job.

1386
01:45:09,262 --> 01:45:12,384
Mistake three, expecting silence while it works.

1387
01:45:12,624 --> 01:45:16,516
With the thinking model, just because it finished a sentence doesn't mean it's done.

1388
01:45:16,784 --> 01:45:19,104
It might still be working away in the background.

1389
01:45:19,184 --> 01:45:20,784
So don't cut it off too early.

1390
01:45:20,944 --> 01:45:21,668
Give it a beep.

1391
01:45:22,224 --> 01:45:25,988
Alright, three quick pro tips to actually get value out of this.

1392
01:45:26,304 --> 01:45:29,104
Tip one, pick the right model on purpose.

1393
01:45:29,422 --> 01:45:32,644
Fast and simple, use Gemini 3.8 Live.

1394
01:45:32,864 --> 01:45:35,492
Hard and layered, use extended thinking.

1395
01:45:35,744 --> 01:45:37,988
Don't just grab the biggest one out of habit.

1396
01:45:38,464 --> 01:45:41,424
Tip two, lean into the let me check moment.

1397
01:45:41,870 --> 01:45:44,944
The whole magic here is that it keeps talking while it works.

1398
01:45:45,104 --> 01:45:47,264
So build your conversations around that.

1399
01:45:47,424 --> 01:45:49,824
Let it acknowledge you, then go do the task.

