2425
03:08:14,544 --> 03:08:19,184
A minute of setup is the difference between something you're proud to share and something you delete.

2426
03:08:19,470 --> 03:08:20,704
So what can you actually set?

2427
03:08:20,864 --> 03:08:28,064
Quite a lot. You can choose your output language, you can pick the level of detail, concise, standard, or detailed, you can set the orientation,

2428
03:08:28,224 --> 03:08:31,344
square, portrait, or landscape, depending on where you plan to use it.

2429
03:08:31,504 --> 03:08:35,332
There are visual styles you can pick from, or you can let it auto select to look for you.

2430
03:08:35,566 --> 03:08:44,544
And then there's the most powerful control of all, the text box, where you describe in your own words exactly what you want the infographic to show and how you want it to feel.

2431
03:08:44,782 --> 03:08:50,224
Let me give you some real examples of what you can type into that box because this is where the magic happens.

2432
03:08:50,414 --> 03:08:58,704
On the content side, you could say create a timeline of the key events described in this source, or compare the pros and cons mentioned in the documents.

2433
03:08:58,894 --> 03:09:03,824
Those instructions shape what information ends up on the page. Then you can layer on the look.

2434
03:09:03,984 --> 03:09:13,104
You could say use a blue color theme and highlight the three key stats, or push the style further with something like bento grid layout, clean design, professional colours,

2435
03:09:13,344 --> 03:09:14,624
minimalist icons.

2436
03:09:14,862 --> 03:09:22,944
You can even ask for very specific aesthetics: a soft, high-tech look, a hand-drawn whiteboard style, a chalkboard feel, whatever fits your message.

2437
03:09:23,118 --> 03:09:31,492
That text box is where your infographic goes from looking like everybody else's default output to something that actually stands out and feels like yours.

2438
03:09:31,758 --> 03:09:33,988
Here's something worth knowing before you even generate.

2439
03:09:34,304 --> 03:09:38,464
The quality of your infographic depends heavily on how clear your source is.

2440
03:09:38,638 --> 03:09:47,744
If your original document jumps around, skips steps, or mixes up causes and effects, the infographic will look confused too, because it's only working with what you gave it.

2441
03:09:47,950 --> 03:09:51,184
So if you're getting messy results, don't blame the tool right away.

2442
03:09:51,344 --> 03:09:53,892
Take a look at whether the source itself is well organized.

2443
03:09:54,094 --> 03:09:55,812
Clean input, clean output.

2444
03:09:55,984 --> 03:10:01,984
That's true for every tool in the studio, but it shows up the most with visuals because you can literally see the confusion on the page.

2445
03:10:02,144 --> 03:10:10,212
Once you've set it up and hit generate, it builds in the background. So you can keep working on other things while it does its thing. You don't have to sit and stare at a loading screen.

2446
03:10:10,384 --> 03:10:19,344
It usually takes a couple of minutes. When it's ready, you can open it up in a bigger viewer, zoom in to check the details, download it as a PNG file and share it.

2447
03:10:19,438 --> 03:10:25,344
