4784
05:58:55,344 --> 05:59:01,024
Now I promised you a prompt trick, so let me give it to you because this one changes your image results instantly.

4785
05:59:01,184 --> 05:59:06,944
Most people type something lazy like make an image of a woman in a red dress, and then they're confused when it looks generic.

4786
05:59:07,150 --> 05:59:08,864
The fix is simple. Be specific.

4787
05:59:09,024 --> 05:59:09,984
Stack the details.

4788
05:59:10,144 --> 05:59:15,104
Instead of that lazy prompt, try something like a young woman in a red dress running through a park.

4789
05:59:15,342 --> 05:59:15,984
See the difference?

4790
05:59:16,238 --> 05:59:18,756
You're giving it the subject, the action, and the scene.

4791
05:59:18,958 --> 05:59:22,224
So here's the easy formula to remember subject, action, scene.

4792
05:59:22,382 --> 05:59:23,584
Then keep adding detail.

4793
05:59:23,758 --> 05:59:27,824
Tell it the style, tell it the mood, tell it the aspect ratio if you want a certain shape.

4794
05:59:28,014 --> 05:59:30,820
The more you feed it, the closer it gets to what's in your head.

4795
05:59:31,054 --> 05:59:34,464
That one habit alone makes your images look way more professional.

4796
05:59:34,702 --> 05:59:37,024
And here's a bonus tip for total beginners.

4797
05:59:37,184 --> 05:59:39,172
Don't try to get it perfect on the first try.

4798
05:59:39,424 --> 05:59:41,344
Generate something, then just talk to it.

4799
05:59:41,550 --> 05:59:42,852
Tell it to change the background.

4800
05:59:43,054 --> 05:59:43,876
Swap an object.

4801
05:59:44,110 --> 05:59:47,076
Add an element, it keeps the parts you like and fixes the rest.

4802
05:59:47,310 --> 05:59:49,892
Treat it like a conversation, not a vending machine.

4803
05:59:50,094 --> 05:59:52,464
